1. LicenseRef-UEI-Proprietary
-------------------------------
   Built into libUeiPal.a:
   AsyncDelegate.cpp          CircularBuffer.cpp
   ClockWatch.cpp             HighResTimer.cpp
   Pipe.cpp                   SignalGenerator.cpp
   SynchObj.cpp               Thread.cpp
   UeiDaqPAL.cpp              UeiPalTest/UeiPalTest.cpp

   Installed files:
   /usr/include/AsyncDelegate.h    /usr/include/CircularBuffer.h
   /usr/include/ClockWatch.h       /usr/include/HighResTimer.h
   /usr/include/Pipe.h             /usr/include/SignalGenerator.h
   /usr/include/StdAfx.h           /usr/include/SynchObj.h
   /usr/include/Thread.h           /usr/include/UeiDaqPAL.h
   /usr/lib/libUeiPal.a            /usr/local/sbin/UeiPalTest

   [REVIEW NOTE - remove before commit] Almost none of the UEI files have a
   copyright or license header today. Add the SPDX header shown below to
   each file.


2. LGPL-3.0-or-later
   sxmlc - Simple XML C parser (see sxmlc/COPYING.LESSER.txt)
----------------------
   Built into libUeiPal.a and UeiPalTest:
   sxmlc/sxmlc.c       sxmlc/sxmlsearch.c  sxmlc/sxmlutils.c

   Installed headers:
   /usr/include/sxmlc.h       /usr/include/sxmlsearch.h
   /usr/include/sxmlutils.h

   [REVIEW NOTE - remove before commit] sxmlc is LGPL-3.0-or-later and is
   linked STATICALLY into libUeiPal.a (shipped in ueipallib-staticdev,
   which is in the image) and UeiPalTest. LGPL-3.0 section 4 requires that
   recipients can relink with a modified sxmlc (provide object files or the
   UEI sources) and receive the LGPL/GPL texts and sxmlc source. Consider
   building sxmlc as a shared library or replacing it.


3. LicenseRef-PublicDomain
   written by Tom Torfs, 2002
----------------------------
   Installed header:
   /usr/include/scandir.h


Files not built/installed for the ARM (SoloX) target
----------------------------------------------------
Windows/Visual Studio project files, tests and other build variants in the
SVN module are not part of the Yocto package and are not covered by this
summary.



